       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum for adults:** 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision. The usual single dose is 400\u2013800 mg, and the OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This order is twice the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n- **600 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **A different dose or drug.**\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
